  "workload": "12 synthetic WGSL sources, one third vertex, fragment and compute; approximately 64 KiB or 3 MiB each. Generated with unique unused helper functions; no game material. Harness models the production worker metadata scans: old code resolves the declared stage and only a fragment-stage mask; proposed code resolves all stage entrypoints and a fragment mask, while both parse group 0, all groups and declarations before releasing source storage. Generation and original explicit entry-point extraction are outside the timed region.",
  "sampling": "Seven process-level samples per variant and workload, alternating baseline/patch order. Each scan_ns sums 12 sequential scan durations. Binaries were built before timing; process listing showed no concurrent builds or CPU-intensive work. Source capacity is summed immediately before and after releasing each source. The checksum is a work counter, not proof of rendered output.",
  "commands": [
    "c++ -std=c++20 -O3 -DNDEBUG -I BASE/runtime PATCH/tools/bench_shader_identity.cpp -o bench-base",
    "c++ -std=c++20 -O3 -DNDEBUG -DPROPOSED -I PATCH/runtime PATCH/tools/bench_shader_identity.cpp -o bench-patch",
    "Run each executable with arguments 12 65536 and 12 3145728, alternating order seven times. BASE and PATCH are separate checkouts."
  ],
  "limitations": "Synthetic scanner-model benchmark only: measured before #2167, it excludes the subsequently added binding-access scan and does not measure the complete current worker. No actual native executor, pack I/O, Dawn compilation, GPU, browser, process RSS or game timing. Both variants implement upstream source release, so its memory saving is not a new benefit of this fix. Scan timing depends on shader text shape and does not establish a game or startup speedup. Capacity includes implementation-specific small-string capacity.",
